COMPARE COMPLETE PROPOSITIONS, THEN COMMIT TO THE STATUS
The diff inventory splits sentences into shared and unique fragments. A unique
fragment is not an independent proposition. Read surrounding shared fragments
and the opposite fragments to recover who does what, under which condition, with
what purpose, value or consequence. A different wording can express the same rule.
For each side, coverage_explanation should briefly state its retained proposition
or harmless element, the actual opposite-side counterpart, and why meaning is or
is not retained. Cite the relevant IDs there. No long internal debate.
Only after this comparison fill loss selections, type, relation, mode and final
status. Do not start with a verdict and then argue yourself out of it. If a real
loss remains, consistently encode UNCOVERED; never call it covered to avoid evidence.

ESTABLISH THE ACTUAL RETAINED SUBJECT
In scope_explanation independently identify what A and B represent, including any
specific subject of their retained message. Anchor both sides. Shared owner, brand,
navigation, footer or cookie text does not bind an attached product, person or list.
SAME_SUBSTANTIVE_RECORD requires a nonempty specific record core on EACH side
after site chrome is set aside. An actual product listing versus only shared store
menus is DISTINCT_OR_UNBOUND_RECORDS, not a one-sided extension of a common record.
An organization description, FAQ, recruitment notice or product record may be the
same retained record even if one side adds actual facts or steps.
NON_MAIN_MESSAGES includes consent/auth/error/navigation notices: identify their
actual message purpose, recipient/subject, permission, controller and state.
Names in a menu or an unbound pointer do not automatically identify the page's
retained subject. Names explicitly identifying a profile, recipient, product,
service, author of retained content or actual list member do matter.

FIRST CHECK WHETHER THE CLAIMED LOSS IS ALREADY EXPRESSED
- A says 'By continuing to use this site, you consent to cookies.' B says
  'Continuing your visit means agreement to cookies. Accept | Settings'. Both
  retain continued-use consent. An optional Accept button does not negate B's
  sentence or prove that clicking is required. This applies to paraphrases and
  translations, even when the same sentence is split over several diff IDs.
- Contrast B saying 'No analytics cookies are used until you click Accept'.
  That explicitly changes a retained condition. A button alone does not say this.
- An opportunity to change settings or withdraw consent does not by itself assert
  an opt-in default, a previous consent event, or a mandatory new procedure.
  If one side explicitly specifies a default state and the other does not retain
  it, evaluate that actual omission; do not invent a contrary state to strengthen it.
- Different translation fragments can jointly express the same complete message.
  Faithful translation, reordered sentences, repeated propositions and soft hyphens
  add no retained meaning. Changed purposes, conditions, values or recipients do.

THEN DISTINGUISH A POINTER FROM THE SUBJECT IT ACTUALLY IDENTIFIES
- Same organization/website introduction, with a detached 'Stories...Mira Lane'
  pointer on one side and no story or person-specific proposition: the pointer
  does not make Mira the introduction's subject or add biography facts. It can
  be harmless navigation; do not call every name a substantive extension.
- 'Mira | Private profile. Only approved friends may view this profile' versus
  'Noah | Private profile' with that same restriction: the title identifies whose
  profile the restriction concerns. This is an actual subject difference despite
  identical access text. Do not call both names harmless just because no bio is visible.
- A real person's biography, separate product, named service recipient or actual
  independently listed member is retained. Require the binding to the visible
  record/message, not an imagined page layout.

DO NOT REPLACE MISSING FACTS WITH COMMON KNOWLEDGE
- Same vacancy, but only A specifies 'Apply by emailing Dr. N at hiring@example.org
  with subject Research-7': B's 'Applications welcome' does not supply that person,
  address or required subject. These are real one-sided MAIN_CONTENT additions.
  A spam-protection notice is not an application method.
- Contrast an exact paraphrase/translation of the same contact and instructions:
  the method is covered, not a new procedure. Repeating it twice also adds no method.
- Same FAQ plus a reset step, same product with an additional field: true extension
  when the other side retains that same record core. Changed field values, states,
  actual subjects or list members are conflicts, not simple missing fields.
- Non-main data-use purposes, obligations, definitions, access requirements,
  withdrawal consequences and troubleshooting steps can be real uncovered meaning.
  Shortness, standard wording, shared banner, or absence of contradiction does not
  make those propositions harmless. Ordinary UI offers do not assert a new state.

DIRECTIONS AND STRICT OUTPUT
a_meaning_in_b asks whether B retains ALL of A's meaning; b_meaning_in_a asks
whether A retains ALL of B's meaning. These are not replacement direction names.
Account for every own unique ID in reviewed_unique_ids. A selected source_span_id
is ONE own unique ID locating the decisive loss. Use shared context to understand
the full clause; the program extracts that selected span verbatim, without copying
or correcting quotes. counterpart_span_id is ONE opposite/shared ID actually checked,
or empty if none. It is not a list/range. Explain other losses briefly as well.

CONTRADICTS requires an explicitly contrary opposite proposition. If the opposite
does not state the same fact/condition, use NO_EQUIVALENT_FOUND, not an invented negation.
MAIN_CONTENT means a retained same-record fact/step; POLICY_MEANING a retained
non-main purpose/permission/obligation/definition; RECORD_IDENTITY an actual subject,
recipient/service/controller; PAGE_ROLE an evidenced function; STATE_VERSION a factual
state/version; MEMBERSHIP actual retained members; OTHER_RETAINED another genuine loss.

- UNCOVERED -> NOT_COVERED, non-NONE type, own source ID, retention_consequence and
  NO_EQUIVALENT_FOUND or CONTRADICTS. Partial coverage is not MIXED.
- COVERED -> SEMANTIC_COUNTERPARTS or MIXED with opposite/shared coverage_counterpart_ids
  when meanings have actual counterparts. MIXED is FULL coverage plus harmless UI.
- COVERED -> HARMLESS_ONLY for only harmless unique elements; NO_UNIQUE_SPANS only
  when this side has no unique IDs. Both modes have empty coverage_counterpart_ids.
- COVERED/UNRESOLVED have NONE type, empty source_span_id, counterpart_span_id and
  retention_consequence, and NOT_APPLICABLE counterpart_relation.
- UNRESOLVED uses NOT_COVERED and empty coverage_counterpart_ids. Incomplete review
